---
import Component from "../../layouts/Component.astro"
import DocLink from "../../components/DocLink.astro"
import KeyboardSupport from "./partials/KeyboardSupport.astro"
import Usage from "./partials/Usage.astro"
import AutoExample from "../../components/AutoExample.astro"
import Conditional from "../../components/Conditional.astro"
import PropOrClass from "../../components/PropOrClass.astro"

import CopyCSS from "@opui/css/components/copy.css?raw"
import CopyJS from "@opui/elements/copy.js?raw"

import copyApi from "../../component-api/copy/api"

export const description =
  "A button that copies text or a field's value to the clipboard."
---

<Component
  description={description}
  slug="copy"
  browserSupport={[
    "container-style-queries",
    "display-animation",
    "interest-invokers",
    "invoker-commands",
    "light-dark",
    "overlay",
    "popover",
    "popover-hint",
    "relative-color",
    "starting-style",
    "transition-behavior",
  ]}
  apis={[{ title: "Copy API", api: copyApi }]}
  changelogPaths={[
    { path: "packages/opui/components/Copy/Copy.astro", type: "component" },
    { path: "src/docs/components/copy.astro", type: "docs" },
    { path: "src/component-examples/copy", type: "docs" },
    { path: "packages/opui/css/components/copy.css", type: "css" },
    { path: "packages/opui/elements/copy.js", type: "component" },
    { path: "src/component-api/copy", type: "api" },
  ]}
  installationTabs={[
    { title: "copy.css", code: CopyCSS, lang: "css" },
    { title: "copy.js", code: CopyJS, lang: "js" },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Copy</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    <p>
      A button that copies text or a field's value to the clipboard. The <code
        >&lt;opui-copy&gt;</code
      > custom element wraps what to copy, and any <DocLink
        href="/components/button">Button</DocLink
      > points at it with <code>commandfor</code> and <code
        >command="--copy"</code
      >.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Usage slot="usage">
    <li slot="when">
      A value people paste somewhere else, like an <a href="#basics"
        >invite link</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li slot="when">
      A command or a snippet people run, like an <a href="#snippet"
        >install command</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li slot="when-not">
      Confirming something that happened elsewhere, like saved changes. Use a <DocLink
        href="/components/toast">Toast</DocLink
      >.
    </li>
    <li slot="when-not">
      Text people edit before they use it, like a message. Use a <DocLink
        href="/components/textarea">Textarea</DocLink
      >, which people copy from themselves.
    </li>
  </Usage>

  <section>
    <h2 id="basics">Basics</h2>
    <Conditional as="div">
      <p slot="components">
        Wrap the field or the text in <code>Copy</code> with an <code>id</code>,
        and give a <code>Button</code>
        <code>commandfor</code> with that id and
        <code>command="--copy"</code>. A field's value is copied, otherwise the
        text. A label in the look of an outlined button says "Copied" next to
        the button for two seconds, and a screen reader hears it; <code
          >copiedLabel</code
        > changes the words.
      </p>
      <p slot="html">
        Wrap the field or the text in <code
          >&lt;opui-copy class="ui-copy"&gt;</code
        > with an id, end it with <code
          >&lt;span class="ui-sr-only" role="status"&gt;</code
        > and <code
          >&lt;span class="ui-floating" popover aria-hidden="true"&gt;</code
        >, give a button <code>commandfor</code> with that id and <code
          >command="--copy"</code
        >, and import <code>opui-css/elements/copy.js</code>. A field's value is
        copied, otherwise the text. The label in the look of an outlined button
        says "Copied" next to the button for two seconds, and a screen reader
        hears it; <code>copied-label</code> changes the words.
      </p>
    </Conditional>
    <p>
      The label sits before the button at the button's height, with its font and
      corners, or after it when there's no room. The button itself doesn't
      change. Set <code>--ui-anchor-position-area</code> on the element to move the
      label.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Basics" row />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="snippet">Snippet</h2>
    <p>
      The button can sit inside the element too. Buttons and popovers are left
      out of the copied text, so an icon button with a <DocLink
        href="/components/tooltip">Tooltip</DocLink
      > next to the code is fine. The label takes the tooltip's place, and the tooltip
      stays closed while the label shows.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Snippet" row />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="failed">Failed copy</h2>
    <Conditional as="div">
      <p slot="components">
        Where the page has no Clipboard API, like without HTTPS, or the
        clipboard refuses or doesn't answer within two seconds, the element
        copies through a selection instead. Where that is blocked too, the label
        says "Copy failed" until Esc, a click elsewhere or the next press, and
        the text is selected so people can copy it themselves. A field also gets
        focus, so the keyboard shortcut copies it. <code>failedLabel</code> changes
        the words.
      </p>
      <p slot="html">
        Where the page has no Clipboard API, like without HTTPS, or the
        clipboard refuses or doesn't answer within two seconds, the element
        copies through a selection instead. Where that is blocked too, the label
        says "Copy failed" until Esc, a click elsewhere or the next press, and
        the text is selected so people can copy it themselves. A field also gets
        focus, so the keyboard shortcut copies it. <code>failed-label</code> changes
        the words.
      </p>
    </Conditional>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="without-javascript">Without JavaScript</h2>
    <p>
      Until <code>copy.js</code> loads, a copy button inside the element or right
      after it is hidden, and the text can still be selected. Put the button in one
      of those places, or hide it yourself. <PropOrClass
        prop="Copy"
        class=".ui-copy"
      /> has <code>display: contents</code>, so it doesn't change the layout.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="accessibility">
    <ul>
      <li>
        The announcement goes through a polite live region inside the element,
        so it doesn't interrupt. The button keeps its name.
      </li>
      <li>
        The label has <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>, since the live region
        already announces its words.
      </li>
      <li>
        Where the clipboard is blocked, the element announces the failure and
        selects the text instead, so people can copy it themselves.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <KeyboardSupport />
  </Fragment>
</Component>
